From: Codex <codex@openai.local>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 21:56:55 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] A single lost git spawn is not "git is absent", and it
 refused to trade 25 times today

`release_identity._git` gave every call one attempt. On the trading box -- 118 python processes,
a dozen git processes, one repository -- the spawn sometimes just loses, and the gateway then
recorded

    RELEASE IDENTITY refuses NEW risk: running <sha> != sealed <sha> and the diff cannot be
    taken (git absent, or the sealed commit is not in this clone)

25 times on 2026-09-24 alone, at up to 5 an hour. The wording is self-diagnosing: `verdict`
writes "git absent" only when `source != "git"`, i.e. `git rev-parse HEAD` returned nothing and
the SHA had to be recovered by reading `.git` directly. git was installed and the sealed commit
was present every time. One lost spawn skipped the diff entirely and the pass refused new risk.

This is the same class as the stale seal and the ten-second timeout: a rail refusing on a
question nobody actually answered. Retrying MEASURES more, it does not PERMIT more -- an identity
that genuinely cannot be measured still refuses, and three consecutive failures on a machine
where git works is a real fault worth refusing on. Bounded: three attempts, 0.4s then 0.8s apart,
once per pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WZHzZoD3QX9Tx668fkAaw6
